# Merge to master

Integrate topic branches with a **fast-forward only** merge onto `master`.
Never `git merge --no-ff`. Never create a merge commit on `master`.

Use [`merge-to-master.sh`](merge-to-master.sh) from a clean topic branch:

```bash
bash merge-to-master.sh
```

The script fetches `origin`, checks that `master` is an ancestor of `HEAD`,
switches to `master`, then `git merge --ff-only`. It does not push.

If fast-forward is impossible, rebase the topic onto `master` first, then
rerun the script. Do not merge `master` into the topic as the landing step.

Do not push `master` unless the user asks.
